      "agent_input": "Please read the Excel file at CUGA_generalist_agent/.cuga/env/testbed/data/order_summary.xlsx, extract all cell contents, and save them to a new file for my review.",
      "agent_response": {
        "response": "[Awaiting tool approval]\n\n**Policy:** Shell command approval (skills demo)\nAbout to run a shell command in the agent workspace. Approve to continue?\n**Required Tools:** run_command\n```python\nfiles = await list_files(\"CUGA_generalist_agent/.cuga/env/testbed/data/\")\nprint(files)\n\nfile_info = await get_file_info(\"CUGA_generalist_agent/.cuga/env/testbed/data/order_summary.xlsx\")\nprint(file_info)\n\nskill_text = await load_skill(\"OfficeBench\")\nprint(skill_text)\n\nresult = await run_command(\"which python3 && python3 --version\")\nprint(result)\n\ninstall_result = await run_command(\"uv pip install openpyxl xlrd\")\nprint(install_result)\n\nimport asyncio\nawait asyncio.sleep(5)\nverify = await run_command('python -c \"import openpyxl; print(\\'ok\\')\"')\nprint(verify)\n\nscript = '''import openpyxl\nimport json\n\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook(\"CUGA_generalist_agent/.cuga/env/testbed/data/order_summary.xlsx\", data_only=True)\n\nall_data = {}\n\nfor sheet_name in wb.sheetnames:\n    ws = wb[sheet_name]\n    sheet_data = []\n    for row in ws.iter_rows(min_row=1, max_row=ws.max_row, max_col=ws.max_column, values_only=False):\n        row_data = []\n        for cell in row:\n            val = cell.value\n            if val is None:\n                row_data.append(\"\")\n            else:\n                row_data.append(str(val))\n        sheet_data.append(row_data)\n    all_data[sheet_name] = {\n        \"max_row\": ws.max_row,\n        \"max_col\": ws.max_column,\n        \"rows\": sheet_data\n    }\n\nprint(json.dumps(all_data, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n'''\nawait write_file(\"./read_excel.py\", script)\nprint(\"Script written.\")\n\nexcel_output = await run_command(\"python ./read_excel.py\")\nprint(excel_output[:5000])\n\nimport json\n\ndata = json.loads(excel_output)\n\nlines = []\nfor sheet_name, info in data.items():\n    lines.append(f\"===== Sheet: {sheet_name} =====\")\n    lines.append(f\"Dimensions: {info['max_row']} rows x {info['max_col']} columns\")\n    lines.append(\"\")\n    \n    rows = info[\"rows\"]\n    if not rows:\n        lines.append(\"(empty sheet)\")\n        lines.append(\"\")\n        continue\n    \n    # Calculate column widths for nice formatting\n    col_count = max(len(r) for r in rows)\n    col_widths = [0] * col_count\n    for r in rows:\n        for i, val in enumerate(r):\n            col_widths[i] = max(col_widths[i], len(val))\n    \n    # Cap column widths at 40 for readability\n    col_widths = [min(w, 40) for w in col_widths]\n    \n    # Build header separator\n    sep = \"+\".join(\"-\" * (w + 2) for w in col_widths)\n    sep = \"+\" + sep + \"+\"\n    \n    for idx, r in enumerate(rows):\n        padded = []\n        for i, val in enumerate(r):\n            w = col_widths[i] if i < len(col_widths) else 10\n            padded.append(f\" {val:<{w}} \")\n        line = \"|\" + \"|\".join(padded) + \"|\"\n        if idx == 0:\n            lines.append(sep)\n        lines.append(line)\n        if idx == 0:\n            lines.append(sep)\n    lines.append(sep)\n    lines.append(\"\")\n\ncontent = \"\\n\".join(lines)\nprint(f\"Generated {len(lines)} lines of formatted output. Preview:\\n\")\nprint(content[:3000])\n\nawait write_file(\"./output/order_summary_extracted.txt\", content)\nprint(\"File saved to ./output/order_summary_extracted.txt\")\n\nverification = await read_file(\"./output/order_summary_extracted.txt\")\nprint(verification)\n```",
